  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wadajir nabadeed: trust, justice and security in newly recovered areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Wadajir Nabadeed (meaning &quot;Together for Peace&quot;) supports peace and stability in areas of Somalia that have been newly or recently recovered from al Shabaab. The project works with the Federal Government of Somalia, Federal Member States, local administrations, and communities, to help restore trust between authorities and citizens and to strengthen the foundations for longer term recovery. The project focuses on three closely linked areas: interim local governance, community safety, and access to justice. It supports government led processes while ensuring that communities, including women, youth, persons with disabilities, minorities, and other marginalized groups, are actively involved in dialogue and decision making. By bringing together local authorities, security actors, and community representatives, Wadajir Nabadeed helps address local tensions, improve cooperation, and support fair and practical ways to resolve disputes by re establishing credible and inclusive government presence at district level, enable the delivery of basic services, and strengthen the relationship between communities and the state. The project is funded by the UN Peacebuilding Fund, implemented by UNDP and IOM Somalia, and is aligned with Somalia&apos;s National Reconciliation Framework and National Stabilization Strategy. It also supports the transfer of stabilization responsibilities from UNTMIS, in line with UN Security Council Resolution 2753.</narrative>
  </description>
